  "hints": [
    "Try the all-pairs brute force first and note its complexity for n = 2*10^5.",
    "After sorting, which pairs can possibly be the closest? Could a non-adjacent pair beat every adjacent pair?",
    "Sort, then take the minimum difference of neighbours. Use a 64-bit type to be safe: the difference can reach 2*10^9."
  ],
  "editorial": "**Brute force:** check every pair, `O(n^2)`. At `n = 2*10^5` that is `2*10^10` operations, too slow, so the constraints are telling us to look for `O(n log n)`.\n\n**Key fact:** after sorting, if `x <= y <= z` then `z - x >= y - x` and `z - x >= z - y`, so a pair that skips an element is never strictly better than one of the adjacent pairs it spans. Hence only neighbours in sorted order matter.\n\nSort and scan neighbours. The largest possible answer is `2*10^9`, which is close to the 32-bit limit, so use `long long` for the subtraction.",
  "complexity": {
    "time": "O(n log n)",
    "space": "O(n)"
  },
  "starter": {
    "python": "# Read n, then n integers. Print the minimum |a_i - a_j| for i != j.\nn = int(input())\na = list(map(int, input().split()))\n# your code here\n",
    "javascript": "const n = parseInt(readLine());\nconst a = readLine().split(' ').map(Number);\n// your code here\n",
    "cpp": "#include <bits/stdc++.h>\nusing namespace std;\n\nint main() {\n    ios::sync_with_stdio(false);\n    cin.tie(nullptr);\n    // read the input and print the answer\n}\n",
    "java": "import java.util.*;\nimport java.io.*;\n\npublic class Main {\n    public static void main(String[] args) throws IOException {\n        BufferedReader br = new BufferedReader(new InputStreamReader(System.in));\n        // read the input and print the answer\n    }\n}\n"
  },
  "solutions": {
    "python": "n = int(input())\na = sorted(map(int, input().split()))\nprint(min(a[i + 1] - a[i] for i in range(n - 1)))\n",
    "javascript": "const n = parseInt(readLine());\nconst a = readLine().split(' ').map(Number).sort((x, y) => x - y);\nlet best = Infinity;\nfor (let i = 0; i + 1 < n; i++) best = Math.min(best, a[i + 1] - a[i]);\nconsole.log(String(best));\n",
    "java": "import java.util.*;\nimport java.io.*;\n\npublic class Main {\n    public static void main(String[] args) throws IOException {\n        BufferedReader br = new BufferedReader(new InputStreamReader(System.in));\n        int n = Integer.parseInt(br.readLine().trim());\n        StringTokenizer st = new StringTokenizer(br.readLine());\n        long[] a = new long[n];\n        for (int i = 0; i < n; i++) a[i] = Long.parseLong(st.nextToken());\n        Arrays.sort(a);\n        long best = Long.MAX_VALUE;\n        for (int i = 0; i + 1 < n; i++) best = Math.min(best, a[i + 1] - a[i]);\n        System.out.println(best);\n    }\n}\n",
    "cpp": "#include <bits/stdc++.h>\nusing namespace std;\nint main() {\n    ios::sync_with_stdio(false);\n    cin.tie(nullptr);\n    int n;\n    cin >> n;\n    vector<long long> a(n);\n    for (auto &x : a) cin >> x;\n    sort(a.begin(), a.end());\n    long long best = LLONG_MAX;\n    for (int i = 0; i + 1 < n; i++) best = min(best, a[i + 1] - a[i]);\n    cout << best << \"\\n\";\n}\n"
  }
